@node Installing Arch
@section Installing Arch
@anchor{#installing-arch}
Details about setting up Arch Linux. PADS has a built in Arch Install
script. Use it at your own risk.

@enumerate 
@item
Boot Mode@*
Verify boot mode. If this command runs with no errors, you're using EFI
Mode.@*
@code{ls /sys/firmware/efi/efivars}

@item
Internet Connection@*
Connect to the internet. If you're on Ethernet, it should be connected
automatically.

@enumerate 
@item
Enable and start
@uref{https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/dhcpcd,,dhcpcd.service}@*
@code{systemctl enable dhcpcd.service}@*
@code{systemctl start dhcpcd.service}@*
@item
If you're on WIFI, use
@uref{https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Iwd#iwctl,,iwd}.@*
@code{iwctl}@*
@code{device list}@*
@code{station device scan}@*
@code{station device get-networks}@*
@code{station device connect SSID}@*
@item
Ping something@dots{}@*
@code{ping www.google.com}
@end enumerate

@item
System Clock@*
Update system clock@*
@code{timedatectl set-ntp true}@*
@code{timedatectl set-timezone America/New_York}@*
@code{timedatectl status}

@item
Partition@*
Partition the disk. I use
@uref{https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/fdisk,,fdisk}. DO NOT OVERWRITE
REDUNDANT STORAGE!!!! List devices, and choose your device.@*
@code{fdisk -l}@*
@code{fdisk /dev/sda}

@enumerate 
@item
EFI Boot Mode:
@enumerate 
@item
Build partition table@*
@code{n} /mnt/boot partition@*
@code{p} primary partition@*
@code{1} /dev/sda1@*
@code{""} first block default@*
@code{+512M} last block 512mb@*
@code{n} swap partition@*
@code{p} primary partition@*
