There isn't much to say. This is something already well
@uref{https://qtile.org/,,documented}.

@enumerate 
@item
Start by installing it, and picom for dynamic windows:@*
@code{sudo pacman -Syu xorg xorg-server xorg-apps xorg-xinit xterm qtile picom}
@end enumerate

@quotation
[!NOTE] The default config is loaded from
@emph{~/.config/qtile/config.py}. If it's not there, copy it from
@emph{/usr/share/doc/qtile/default_config.py}. The config for picom is
at @emph{/etc/xdg/picom.conf}.
@end quotation
@enumerate 2
@item
Change ~/.xinitrc to add the following line:@*
@code{sudo nano ~/.xinitrc}@*
@code{picom &}@*
@code{exec qtile start}@*
@item
Install the qtile-extras to make the bar look cool: It's only on the
AUR@*
@code{cd ~/Downloads}@*
@code{sudo git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/qtile-extras-git.git}@*
@code{cd qtile-extras}@*
